.TH SMSHEET 1
.SH NAME
smsheet \- lay views on sheets as PostScript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smsheet
.I part.draw
.IR views | \-
.br
.B smsheet \-v
.I part.draw
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Smsheet
reads a drawing file,
.IR draw (5),
and views from
.IR smdim (1)
in the file
.IR views ,
or on the standard input for
.B \-
(one per view record, in order, each at the scale of its record),
and writes a PostScript page for each sheet: the template, the views,
and on sheet 1 the notes.
A drawing is made by one pipe:
.PP
.RS
.nf
smsheet \-v part.draw | smview part.st | smdim |
	smsheet part.draw \- > part.ps
.fi
.RE
.PP
The scale of a sheet, in its title block, is that of its first view;
a view at another scale gets its scale under it.
The views of a sheet must fit the template and, below scale 1, no
ordinate text may stand more than .75 in from its place.
The views of a sheet are arranged in third-angle projection around the
front view, .4 in apart and .25 in clear of the notes and the kept
regions; a view with
.B at
is placed at the given point.
.PP
The lettering is osifont, to be found by Ghostscript with
.BI \-sFONTPATH= dir ,
as in the fonts of the library,
.IR plicad-lib (7).
.TP
.B \-v
Print the views of the drawing file for
.IR smview (1):
a line
.BI units " unit unit"
(the second \- if none),
.BI unmarked " material"
or
.BR "unmarked \-" ,
and for each view, after a line
.BI #line " n file"
of its record, a line
.BI view " name"
.BR \-h | \-
.I scale
.IR depth | \-
(whether it shows hidden lines, its scale, and the depth of its cut in
mm), and each of its records for
.IR smdim (1)
after it, its lengths in inches, after a line
.BI #line " n file" .
.SH SEE ALSO
draw(5), smview(1), smdim(1), gs(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
FILE:LINE: and the fault, for a bad record of the drawing file, as a
.B lin
with a tolerance of its own, which the model gives
.RI ( draw (5)).
If the views of a sheet do not fit, their size is given with the room
of the template.
